#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to use stretch to defer timing resolution with dynamic circuits"
msgstr "Comment utiliser stretch pour différer la résolution du timing avec les circuits dynamiques"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch"
msgstr "Résolution différée du timing avec stretch"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deferred timing resolution using stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"
msgstr "Résolution différée du timing avec stretch {#deferred-timing-resolution-using-stretch}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The OpenQASM 3 language specification contains a `stretch` type with which you can specify relative timing of operations instead of absolute timing. Support for `stretch` as durations for [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) instructions was added in [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). The concrete value of a stretch duration is resolved at compile time, after the exact duration of calibrated gates are known.  The compiler tries to minimize the stretch duration, subject to timing constraints on one or more qubits. You can then express gate designs such as evenly spacing gates (for example, to implement a higher-order echo decoupling sequence), left-aligning a sequence of gates, or applying a gate for the duration of some sub-circuit, without knowing the exact timing.\n"
msgstr "La spécification du langage OpenQASM 3 comprend un type `stretch` qui permet de définir le timing relatif des opérations plutôt qu'un timing absolu. La prise en charge de `stretch` comme durée pour les instructions [`Delay`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#qiskit.circuit.Delay) a été ajoutée dans [Qiskit v2.0.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes/2.0#200). La valeur concrète d'une durée stretch est résolue à la compilation, une fois que les durées exactes des portes calibrées sont connues. Le compilateur cherche à minimiser la durée stretch, sous réserve des contraintes de timing sur un ou plusieurs qubits. Tu peux ainsi exprimer des agencements de portes tels que l'espacement uniforme de portes (par exemple pour implémenter une séquence d'écho de découplage d'ordre supérieur), l'alignement à gauche d'une séquence de portes, ou l'application d'une porte pour la durée d'un sous-circuit, sans connaître le timing exact.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr "Exemples {#examples}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Découplage dynamique {#dynamical-decoupling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common use case of `stretch` is to apply dynamical decoupling to an idling qubit while another qubit is undergoing conditional operations.\n"
msgstr "Un cas d'usage courant de `stretch` consiste à appliquer un découplage dynamique à un qubit inactif pendant qu'un autre qubit effectue des opérations conditionnelles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, we can use `stretch` to apply an XX dynamical decoupling sequence to qubit 1, for the duration of the conditional block applied to qubit 0, as illustrated by the following diagram:\n"
msgstr "Par exemple, on peut utiliser `stretch` pour appliquer une séquence de découplage dynamique XX au qubit 1, pour la durée du bloc conditionnel appliqué au qubit 0, comme illustré par le diagramme suivant :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Image illustrating the following circuit](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Image illustrant le circuit suivant](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The corresponding circuit would look like the following. Note that a pair of barriers is needed to define the boundaries of this relative timing.\n"
msgstr "Le circuit correspondant ressemble à ce qui suit. Note qu'une paire de barrières est nécessaire pour définir les limites de ce timing relatif.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scheduling alignment {#scheduling-alignment}"
msgstr "Alignement de la planification {#scheduling-alignment}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example uses `stretch` to ensure a sequence of gates between two barriers are left-aligned, whatever their actual durations are:\n"
msgstr "Cet exemple utilise `stretch` pour garantir qu'une séquence de portes entre deux barrières est alignée à gauche, quelles que soient leurs durées réelles :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid " When using `stretch` with IBM Quantum Compute Service, any remainder resulting from a stretch resolution is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgstr " Lors de l'utilisation de `stretch` avec IBM Quantum Compute Service, tout reste résultant d'une résolution stretch est ajouté au premier délai qui utilise le stretch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example:\n"
msgstr "Exemple :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"
msgstr ""
"    ```python\n"
"    a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"    circuit.delay(100, q0)\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 26\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.delay(a, q1)  # resolve to 25\n"
"    circuit.x(q1)  # duration: 8\n"
"    circuit.barrier(q0, q1)\n"
"     ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The above code resolves to a value of 25 with a remainder of 1. The first delay`[a]` will have the remainder added.\n"
msgstr "Le code ci-dessus est résolu à une valeur de 25 avec un reste de 1. Le premier délai `[a]` se verra ajouter ce reste.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stretch resolution equation:  $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"
msgstr "Équation de résolution du stretch : $a + 8 + a + 8 + a + 8 = 100   =   3*a + 24$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr "</DoqAdmonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "View stretch values in IBM Quantum Compute Service {#view-stretch-values-in-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "Afficher les valeurs stretch dans IBM Quantum Compute Service {#view-stretch-values-in-ibm-quantum-compute-service}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The actual value of a stretch duration is resolved at compile time, after the circuit is scheduled. When running a Sampler job in IBM Quantum Compute Service, you can view the resolved stretch values in the job result metadata.  Support for `stretch` in Quantum Compute is currently experimental, so you need to first set an experimental option to enable its retrieval, then access the data directly from the metadata as follows:\n"
msgstr "La valeur réelle d'une durée stretch est résolue à la compilation, après la planification du circuit. Lors de l'exécution d'un job Sampler dans IBM Quantum Compute Service, tu peux consulter les valeurs stretch résolues dans les métadonnées du résultat du job. La prise en charge de `stretch` dans Quantum Compute est actuellement expérimentale ; tu dois donc d'abord activer une option expérimentale pour en permettre la récupération, puis accéder aux données directement depuis les métadonnées comme suit :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Although the total circuit time is returned in the \"compilation\" metadata, this is NOT the time used for billing (QPU time).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Bien que le temps total du circuit soit renvoyé dans les métadonnées « compilation », il ne s'agit PAS du temps utilisé pour la facturation (temps QPU).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the metadata output {#understand-the-metadata-output}"
msgstr "Comprendre la sortie des métadonnées {#understand-the-metadata-output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `stretch_values` metadata returns the following information:\n"
msgstr "Les métadonnées `stretch_values` renvoient les informations suivantes :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Name:** The name of the applied stretch.\n"
msgstr "**Name :** Le nom du stretch appliqué.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Value:** The requested goal value.\n"
msgstr "**Value :** La valeur cible demandée.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Remainder:** The remainder from resolving the stretch, which is added to the first delay that uses the stretch.\n"
msgstr "**Remainder :** Le reste de la résolution du stretch, qui est ajouté au premier délai utilisant ce stretch.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Expanded values:** Sets of values that specify the stretch start and its duration.\n"
msgstr "**Expanded values :** Des ensembles de valeurs précisant le début du stretch et sa durée.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Exemple {#example}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Metadata output {#metadata-output}"
msgstr "Sortie des métadonnées {#metadata-output}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The values returned for duration depend on the goal value and the calculated remainder.  For example, these are the durations returned for foo:\n"
msgstr "Les valeurs renvoyées pour la durée dépendent de la valeur cible et du reste calculé. Par exemple, voici les durées renvoyées pour foo :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` + `remainder` (8+2 = 10) \n"
msgstr "`foo value` + `remainder` (8+2 = 10)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` * 3 (8 x 3 = 24)\n"
msgstr "`foo value` * 3 (8 x 3 = 24)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`foo value` * 2 (8 x 2 = 16)\n"
msgstr "`foo value` * 2 (8 x 2 = 16)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use a visualization to help understand and verify the timing. \n"
msgstr "Tu peux utiliser une visualisation pour mieux comprendre et vérifier le timing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following image, based on the example output, `foo` corresponds to the stretches on Qubit 2. The first stretch delay that uses `foo` starts at the end of the `init_play` (1365). The stretch duration is 10, so that delay ends when the `x` gate starts (1365+10=1375). You can interpret the second and third stretches similarly.\n"
msgstr "Dans l'image suivante, basée sur l'exemple de sortie, `foo` correspond aux stretches sur le qubit 2. Le premier délai stretch utilisant `foo` commence à la fin du `init_play` (1365). La durée du stretch est de 10, donc ce délai se termine au démarrage de la porte `x` (1365+10=1375). Tu peux interpréter les deuxième et troisième stretches de la même façon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The output from the `draw_circuit_schedule_timing` command is shown.](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch-visualization.avif)\n"
msgstr "![La sortie de la commande `draw_circuit_schedule_timing` est affichée.](/docs/images/guides/stretch/stretch-visualization.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the sliders at the bottom, the controls at the top (hover over your output image to reveal these), and the legend on the side of the output to customize the view. Hover over the image to view exact data.\n"
msgstr "Utilise les curseurs en bas, les contrôles en haut (survole ton image de sortie pour les révéler) et la légende sur le côté pour personnaliser la vue. Survole l'image pour voir les données exactes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For full details, see the [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing) topic.\n"
msgstr "Pour tous les détails, consulte la rubrique [Visualiser le timing des circuits](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qiskit-runtime-limitations\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum Compute limitations {#quantum-compute-limitations}"
msgstr "Limitations de Quantum Compute {#quantum-compute-limitations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Support for `stretch` in Quantum Compute is currently experimental and has the following constraints:\n"
msgstr "La prise en charge de `stretch` dans Quantum Compute est actuellement expérimentale et présente les contraintes suivantes :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- At most one stretch variable per _qubit set_ between barriers (implicit and explicit). A qubit set is one or more qubits; these sets must be mutually exclusive.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Au plus une variable stretch par _ensemble de qubits_ entre des barrières (implicites et explicites). Un ensemble de qubits comprend un ou plusieurs qubits ; ces ensembles doivent être mutuellement exclusifs.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q0)  # Invalid because 2 stretches are applied on q0\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q0)  # Invalid because 2 stretches are applied on q0\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q2)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, (q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(b, q2)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- The area surrounded by a set of barriers is called a _barrier region_. A stretch variable cannot be used in multiple barrier regions.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- La zone délimitée par un ensemble de barrières est appelée une _région de barrière_. Une variable stretch ne peut pas être utilisée dans plusieurs régions de barrière.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used in two barrier regions\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used in two barrier regions\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        ![Illustration of the previous code output](/docs/images/guides/stretch/bad-barrier-region.svg 'Invalid use of stretch in barrier regions')\n"
msgstr "        ![Illustration de la sortie du code précédent](/docs/images/guides/stretch/bad-barrier-region.svg 'Invalid use of stretch in barrier regions')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used inside a barrier region that is on q0 and q1\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier(q2)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        # Stretch a is used inside a barrier region that is on q0 and q1\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier(q2)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "        ![Illustration of the previous code output](/docs/images/guides/stretch/good-barrier-region.svg 'Valid use of stretch in a barrier region')\n"
msgstr "        ![Illustration de la sortie du code précédent](/docs/images/guides/stretch/good-barrier-region.svg 'Valid use of stretch in a barrier region')\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions are limited to those of the form `X*stretch + Y` where `X` and `Y` are floating point or integer constants.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Les expressions stretch sont limitées à celles de la forme `X*stretch + Y` où `X` et `Y` sont des constantes en virgule flottante ou entières.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        c = circuit.add_stretch(\"c\")\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        c = circuit.add_stretch(\"c\")\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        # (a /  b) * c is not supported\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.mul(expr.div(a, b), c), q1)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        # (a /  b) * c is not supported\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.mul(expr.div(a, b), c), q1)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        from qiskit.circuit import Duration\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        from qiskit.circuit import Duration\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(expr.mul(a, 2), Duration.dt(3)), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(expr.mul(a, 2), Duration.dt(3)), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions can only include a single stretch variable.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"        <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Les expressions stretch ne peuvent inclure qu'une seule variable stretch.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"        <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, b), 0)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        b = circuit.add_stretch(\"b\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, b), 0)\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, a), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        a = circuit.add_stretch(\"a\")\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, a), 0)\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr "    </Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Stretch expressions cannot resolve to negative delay values. The current solver doesn't infer non-negativity constraints.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"- Les expressions stretch ne peuvent pas se résoudre en valeurs de délai négatives. Le solveur actuel n'infère pas les contraintes de non-négativité.\n"
"    <Tabs>\n"
"         <TabItem value=\"Invalid\" label=\"Invalide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        # The length of this barrier region is 20dt, meaning the\n"
"        # equation for solving stretch 'a' is a + 40dt = 20dt, giving a = -20dt.\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, Duration.dt(40)), q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valid\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        # The length of this barrier region is 20dt, meaning the\n"
"        # equation for solving stretch 'a' is a + 40dt = 20dt, giving a = -20dt.\n"
"        circuit.delay(expr.add(a, Duration.dt(40)), q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"         ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"     <TabItem value=\"Valid\" label=\"Valide\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        ```python\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        ```\n"
"     </TabItem>\n"
"    </Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"        ```python\n"
"        circuit.barrier((q0, q1))\n"
"        circuit.delay(20, q1)\n"
"        circuit.delay(a, q0)\n"
